description:
crate-jmap-base-client/benches/session_and_urls.rs:116-129 uses positional format args:

    accounts.push_str(&format!(
        r#"\"A{:03}\": {{
            \"name\": \"user{}@example.com\",
            ...
        }}"#,
        i, i
    ));

Workspace-wide convention is inline format args — commit 71e9bb2 (style(base-client): inline positional args in error format strings) explicitly swept positional args out of `src/` to enforce the `uninlined_format_args` clippy lint. The bench file added in commit df8c601 was not part of that sweep and re-introduces the pattern.

What goes wrong: clippy::uninlined_format_args fires on this; the workspace pre-commit gate runs `cargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings` which means this fails the gate when benches are included in clippy's scope (cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets). Even if benches are not currently in scope, the inconsistency violates the cookie-cutter discipline (workspace AGENTS.md: 'identical idioms, identical helper names').

Fix: `"A{i:03}"` ... `"user{i}@example.com"` and drop the trailing `, i, i`.

Low priority — mechanical fix, no functional impact.
